freedomnas-profiles (0.9.21-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every edition installs from the package repositories on GitHub, with
    the new Arch/Artix and Void keys
  * Arch and Artix install freedomnas-keyring, which carries the key and
    the repository address

 -- FreedomNAS Team <dev@freedomnas.io>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000

freedomnas-profiles (0.9.20-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Community modules listed, installed and removed from the package
    repository; module checks run next to the WebUI
  * FreeBSD base system as packages (pkgbase) and updates in boot
    environments
  * runit editions managed through runitctl
  * AppJail and dnsmasq for containers on FreeBSD
  * Group share, ACL, Samba, uid and gid renumbering and password expiry
    actions for restores
  * Certificate checked before every WebUI start; supervisor in the
    background and firstboot once per boot
  * Power button handled with acpid where nothing else does; Arch's Samba
    units named smb and nmb

 -- FreedomNAS Team <dev@freedomnas.io>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:28:25 +0000

freedomnas-profiles (0.9.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * UKI backed up before kernel updates, paired with the pre-update
    snapshot, and never activated without zfs.ko
  * Automatic rollback of a kernel update that does not boot
    (92freedomnas-fallback)
  * Every edition installs FreedomNAS from its own repository: Arch and
    Artix from freedomnas-arch, Gentoo from the overlay, FreeBSD from the
    freedomnas-freebsd pkg repository
  * var/tmp, var/spool and FreeBSD's var/crash in datasets of their own
  * Installer diagnostics, read-only pool probing and Gentoo install fixes
  * FreeBSD writes smb4.conf; Debian updates without debconf warnings
  * Virtualization package names on Arch, Artix and Void; diffutils in the
    core packages; multipath left out of the UKI

 -- FreedomNAS Team <dev@freedomnas.io>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:18:58 +0000

freedomnas-profiles (0.9.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NetworkManager on every Linux edition, with the commands for
    checkpoints, interface names, bridges, bonds, VLANs, routes and
    WireGuard
  * Gentoo: zfs compiled against the installed kernel, cpio installed
    before the kernel, no distribution initramfs

